+The <code>_elements</code> parameter consists of a comma-separated list of element names
+or dotted element paths. A simple element name is interpreted as a base element
+defined at the root level in the resource. Dotted paths are interpreted relative
+to the resource being returned, not to the Bundle that contains search or history results.
+For example, <code>_elements=meta.versionId</code> requests <code>Resource.meta.versionId</code>
+on returned resources; it does not request <code>Bundle.meta.versionId</code> from the
+enclosing Bundle. If a dotted path identifies a nested element, the parent elements
+leading to that element are included when the element is returned. <span class="fhir-conformance">Each element
+path component that identifies a choice element SHALL be the base element name without specifying
+<code>[x]</code> or one of the types (e.g., "value" is valid, while "value[x]" and
+"valueQuantity" are not).</span> Clients can expect that
 the elements returned will generally be:
